Subject: [PATCH 0010/0010] serve: ctl - the middle layer the launcher asks for

The launcher does not compute anything: parameters, the VRAM ceiling and the
suggested ctx, preflight warnings and the runtime numbers all come from
`python strata-ctl.py <plan|observe>` -- the new package `strata/ctl`, with
`strata-ctl.py` at the bundle root as the entry point (an embedded CPython with
python311._pth cannot use `-m strata.ctl`).

Also in this patch:
- serve/prepare.py: `--kv-resident 0` means "all KV in VRAM" (the engine's
  default).  The old test treated 0 as streaming, so its log line and its
  RAM-bound ceiling were wrong.

Adds: ctl/params.py (mtp_mode -> mtp/mtp_cpu_moe/spec), ctl/fit.py (capacity
files, ceiling/suggestion, measured slots), ctl/observe.py (log -> slots,
drafts, tok/s, n_ctx), ctl/preflight.py (warnings as codes with priority),
ctl/env.py (CUDA DLLs, sm_86), ctl/tests/ (48 unit tests).

